-- title:
--   Affine dilatation of a finitely generated ideal is of finite type
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $A$ a commutative $R$-algebra which is of finite type over $R$, let $I$ be an ideal of $A$, let $a \in A$, and assume $I$ is finitely generated (`I.FG`). The object in question is [`AffineDilatation.Ring I a`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20), namely the underlying type of the $A$-subalgebra [`AffineDilatation.subalgebra I a`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L17) of the localisation `Localization.Away a` of $A$ at the powers of $a$, this subalgebra being by definition the $A$-subalgebra generated by the subset `gen I a` of $A[1/a]$ attached to $I$ and $a$ (classically, the set of fractions $g/a$ with $g \in I$). The assertion is that this ring, with its induced $R$-algebra structure, is of finite type over $R$: it is a quotient of a polynomial ring in finitely many variables over $R$. No Noetherian hypothesis is imposed on $R$ or $A$; the finite generation of $I$ is assumed separately, as is the finite type of $A$ over $R$.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement underlying the construction of dilatations (blow-ups along a closed subscheme of a fibre) in the theory of Néron models: the dilatation of an affine scheme of finite type is again of finite type. It is used in the construction of the affine charts of a dilatation, via [`NeronModelInfra.exists_isAffineHom_isIso_morphismRestrict_iso_affineDilatation_of_isClosed`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.exists_isAffineHom_isIso_morphismRestrict_iso_affineDilatation_of_isClosed).
